      {
        "description" : "Select the object that you want to load data to. Click Create Target to create the target object the first time the Mapping task runs.\n\nIf the target is a relational target, the Mapping task inserts data into the target table the first time it runs. For subsequent runs, you have the following options:\n1. Keep previously loaded data in the target (default). Select the Insert operation, and disable the Truncate Table option.\n2. Keep only the current data. Select the Insert operation, and enable the Truncate Table option.\n3. Fully reload the target. Select the Insert operation, enable the Truncate Table option, and reset in-out parameter v_max_value to 1.\n\nIf the target is a file target, the Mapping task re-creates the file each time it runs.",
